{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And to Shem was born.</b> A man similar to him in rank was born — namely Eber." "<b>He is also the father of all the children of Eber.</b> Even though those who hold the beliefs of the existence of El, His power, and His providence were called Hebrews (עברים) after Eber, who labored to understand and to teach this — as it says: וַיֻּגַּד לְאַבְרָם הָעִבְרִי (Genesis 14:13) — nevertheless <b>Shem</b> too was the father and teacher of all the children of Eber, for truly a teacher and instructor is called father, as in אֲבִי כָּל תֹּפֵשׂ כִּנּוֹר וְעוּגָב (Genesis 4:21), וּמִי אֲבִיהֶם, and the disciples are called sons, as it says: בְּנֵי הַנְּבִיאִים (I Samuel 10:12)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:46.169313598Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}